Description: Compile aria2 without BitTorrent
 DebridPulse resolves magnets and .torrent files through providers; its aria2
 executor fetches only HTTP(S), FTP and SFTP and never acts as a BitTorrent
 client. Upstream's --disable-bittorrent removes the BitTorrent implementation
 (peer wire, trackers, DHT, PEX, LPD, seeding and every BitTorrent option)
 from the binary instead of merely switching it off at runtime. Metalink and
 every other feature are left exactly as Debian configures them.
 Applied to Debian's own debian/rules with fuzz 0 by build-package.sh.
Author: DebridPulse <https://github.com/Xipher-Zero/debridpulse>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-04
---
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -12,7 +12,8 @@
 		--with-gnutls \
 		--without-openssl \
 		--with-ca-bundle=/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt \
-		--enable-libaria2
+		--enable-libaria2 \
+		--disable-bittorrent
 
 override_dh_auto_install:
 	dh_auto_install
